cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Wormlight, please cite it as below, giving the version you used. Please also cite the connectome it runs:
  Cook et al. 2019, as released in Emmons 2024.
type: software
title: Wormlight
abstract: >-
  A living C. elegans in the browser. The adult hermaphrodite's connectome, run through a graded neuron model and a
  small, documented set of mechanisms the wiring can't supply, drives a physically simulated body on an agar plate on
  the GPU, against a CPU reference. Its behavioural checkpoints were fixed in advance from published measurements.
  Crawling as the first of them asks for it does not yet emerge from the connectome, and the project reports that as
  its result.
authors:
